                    <!-- Sample questions -->
                    <section class="pp-section" id="sample-questions" aria-labelledby="h-sample">
                        <h2 id="h-sample">Try 3 NISM 5D Sample Questions – One From Each Module</h2>
                        <p class="pp-answer">See the type of questions in our NISM V-D tests. Tap an option to check your answer and read the explanation.</p>

                        <div class="pp-q" data-q="1">
                            <p class="pp-q-text" id="pp-q1"><strong>Q1.</strong> What is the lock-in period for investments in an Equity Linked Savings Scheme (ELSS)?</p>
                            <ul class="pp-q-opts" role="group" aria-labelledby="pp-q1">
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">A</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">1 year</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt" data-correct="true"><span class="pp-opt-key">B</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">3 years</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">C</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">5 years</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">D</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">No lock-in</span></button></li>
                            </ul>
                            <p class="pp-q-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                            <div class="pp-q-exp">
                                <p><strong>Correct answer: B – 3 years.</strong> ELSS (Tax Saver) schemes have a lock-in of three years from the date of investment and qualify for deduction under Section 80C under the old tax regime. <em>(Module 1 – Chapter 8: Taxation)</em></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="pp-q" data-q="2">
                            <p class="pp-q-text" id="pp-q2"><strong>Q2.</strong> Nifty is at 24,000. A Nifty call option with a strike price of 23,800 trades at a premium of ₹350. What is the time value of this option?</p>
                            <ul class="pp-q-opts" role="group" aria-labelledby="pp-q2">
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">A</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">₹200</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt" data-correct="true"><span class="pp-opt-key">B</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">₹150</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">C</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">₹350</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">D</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">₹550</span></button></li>
                            </ul>
                            <p class="pp-q-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                            <div class="pp-q-exp">
                                <p><strong>Correct answer: B – ₹150.</strong> Intrinsic value = Spot − Strike = 24,000 − 23,800 = ₹200. Time value = Premium − Intrinsic value = 350 − 200 = ₹150. <em>(Module 2 – Chapter 16: Introduction to Options)</em></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="pp-q" data-q="3">
                            <p class="pp-q-text" id="pp-q3"><strong>Q3.</strong> A bond has a modified duration of 5. If its yield rises by 0.50%, the approximate change in its price is:</p>
                            <ul class="pp-q-opts" role="group" aria-labelledby="pp-q3">
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">A</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">+2.5%</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt" data-correct="true"><span class="pp-opt-key">B</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">−2.5%</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">C</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">−5.0%</span></button></li>
                                <li><button type="button" class="pp-opt"><span class="pp-opt-key">D</span><span class="pp-opt-txt">−0.5%</span></button></li>
                            </ul>
                            <p class="pp-q-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
                            <div class="pp-q-exp">
                                <p><strong>Correct answer: B – about −2.5%.</strong> % change in bond price ≈ − Modified Duration × Change in yield = −5 × 0.50% = −2.5%. Bond prices fall when yields rise. <em>(Module 3 – Chapter 18: Interest Rate, Instruments and Fixed Income Markets)</em></p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

