                        <h3 class="pp-h3">What each module covers</h3>
                        <div class="pp-acc">
                            <details>
                                <summary>Module 1: Mutual Fund Distributors – 68 marks · about 45%</summary>
                                <ul class="pp-chlist"><li><strong>Ch 1: Investment Landscape (5 marks)</strong> – Investors and their goals, saving vs investing, asset classes, investment risks, behavioural biases, risk profiling and asset allocation.</li><li><strong>Ch 2: Concept &amp; Role of a Mutual Fund (4 marks)</strong> – What a mutual fund is, how it works, types of schemes, growth of the industry and where SIFs fit.</li><li><strong>Ch 3: Legal Structure of Mutual Funds in India (3 marks)</strong> – Mutual fund as a trust; roles of the sponsor, trustees, AMC, custodian, RTA and AMFI.</li><li><strong>Ch 4: Legal and Regulatory Framework (7 marks)</strong> – Role of SEBI and other regulators, distributor due diligence, investor complaints (SEBI SCORES) and the AMFI Code of Conduct.</li><li><strong>Ch 5: Scheme Related Information (7 marks)</strong> – Scheme documents (SID, SAI, KIM) and other disclosures, including risk disclosures for SIF strategies.</li><li><strong>Ch 6: Fund Distribution and Channel Management Practices (4 marks)</strong> – Types of distributors, ARN and EUIN, commission and its disclosure, distributor vs investment adviser, change of distributor.</li><li><strong>Ch 7: Net Asset Value, Total Expense Ratio and Pricing of units (5 marks)</strong> – Valuation rules, NAV calculation, TER, IDCW, loads and segregated portfolios. Expect calculation questions.</li><li><strong>Ch 8: Taxation (3 marks)</strong> – Tax on mutual funds and investors, capital gains, IDCW tax, STT, TDS and the ELSS deduction.</li><li><strong>Ch 9: Investor Services (10 marks)</strong> – NFO process, cut-off time, KYC, SIP/SWP/STP, account statements, transactions, service timelines and unclaimed money.</li><li><strong>Ch 10: Risk, Return and Performance of Funds (5 marks)</strong> – Types of risk, return measures, risk measures (standard deviation, beta, Sharpe, Treynor) and credit-risk rules.</li><li><strong>Ch 11: Mutual Fund Scheme Performance (5 marks)</strong> – Benchmarks (price return vs total return index), fund manager performance measures and tracking error.</li><li><strong>Ch 12: Mutual Fund Scheme Selection (10 marks)</strong> – Choosing a scheme by investor needs and risk profile, risk levels, investment styles and comparing schemes. Expect case-based questions.</li></ul>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary>Module 2: Equity Derivatives – 52 marks · about 35%</summary>
                                <ul class="pp-chlist"><li><strong>Ch 13: Basics of Derivatives (10 marks)</strong> – Meaning and types of derivatives, the Indian derivatives market, market participants, exchange-traded vs OTC, and risks in derivatives.</li><li><strong>Ch 14: Understanding Index (5 marks)</strong> – Stock indices, types and attributes of an index, index management, major Indian indices and their uses.</li><li><strong>Ch 15: Introduction to Forwards and Futures (15 marks)</strong> – Forwards and futures, contract specifications, payoff charts, futures pricing (cost of carry), convergence and uses of futures. Expect calculation questions.</li><li><strong>Ch 16: Introduction to Options (13 marks)</strong> – Calls and puts, moneyness, intrinsic and time value, payoff charts, option pricing, Greeks and implied volatility. Expect calculation questions.</li><li><strong>Ch 17: Strategies using Equity Futures and Equity Options (9 marks)</strong> – Hedging, speculation and arbitrage with futures, option strategies, put-call parity and delta hedging.</li></ul>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary>Module 3: Interest Rate Derivatives – 30 marks · 20%</summary>
                                <ul class="pp-chlist"><li><strong>Ch 18: Introduction to Interest Rate, Interest Rate Instruments and Fixed Income Markets (6 marks)</strong> – Interest rate concepts, types of fixed income securities, term structure, yield to maturity, bond pricing, duration and convexity, and India's debt market.</li><li><strong>Ch 19: Interest Rate Derivatives (2 marks)</strong> – Economic role of derivatives, IRD products, market participants, underlyings, and OTC vs exchange-traded IRDs.</li><li><strong>Ch 20: Exchange Traded Interest Rate Futures (10 marks)</strong> – Interest rate futures, payoff charts, contract specifications, lot size and tick value, futures vs FRA, and futures price computation.</li><li><strong>Ch 21: Exchange Traded Interest Rate Options (6 marks)</strong> – Option basics and styles, moneyness, pricing and Greeks, implied volatility, payoff diagrams and IRO contract specifications.</li><li><strong>Ch 22: Strategies using Interest Rate Derivatives (6 marks)</strong> – Hedging bond portfolios with IRDs, option strategies, speculation, arbitrage and spread trading.</li></ul>
                            </details>
                        </div>
                    </section>

