                    <!-- FAQ (matches FAQPage schema exactly) -->
                    <section class="pp-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="h-faq">
                        <h2 id="h-faq">NISM Series V-D FAQs</h2>
                        <div class="pp-acc pp-faq">
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What is the NISM Series V-D exam?</h3></summary>
                                <p>NISM Series V-D is the Mutual Fund – Specialized Investment Fund Distributors Certification Examination, launched by NISM on 22 July 2026. It is the certification for distributors and their associated persons who sell or distribute mutual funds and Specialized Investment Funds (SIFs). The certificate is valid for 3 years.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What is the exam pattern of NISM Series V-D?</h3></summary>
                                <p>The exam has 150 multiple-choice questions of 1 mark each, for 150 marks. You get 3 hours (180 minutes). The questions come from three modules: Mutual Funds (68 marks), Equity Derivatives (52 marks) and Interest Rate Derivatives (30 marks).</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What are the passing marks and negative marking in NISM 5D?</h3></summary>
                                <p>You need 90 marks out of 150 (60%) to pass. There is negative marking of 10% of the marks for each wrong answer, so 0.10 marks are deducted. Because the penalty is small, attempt questions where you can rule out at least one option.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What is the NISM V-D exam fee and how do I register?</h3></summary>
                                <p>NISM lists the exam fee as ₹3,000 plus applicable taxes, with payment gateway charges extra. Register on the NISM portal (cert.nism.ac.in), choose your test centre, date and slot, and pay online. Keep your PAN updated in your NISM profile to get the certificate.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What is the syllabus of NISM Series V-D?</h3></summary>
                                <p>The syllabus has 22 chapters in three modules: all 12 chapters of the NISM V-A Mutual Fund Distributors workbook, the first 5 chapters of the NISM VIII Equity Derivatives workbook, and the first 5 chapters of the NISM IV Interest Rate Derivatives workbook.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Which chapters carry the most marks in NISM V-D?</h3></summary>
                                <p>Introduction to Forwards and Futures (15 marks) and Introduction to Options (13 marks) carry the most. Next come Investor Services, Mutual Fund Scheme Selection, Basics of Derivatives and Exchange Traded Interest Rate Futures at 10 marks each.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Do I need NISM V-D if I already passed V-A and Series XIII?</h3></summary>
                                <p>As reported on SEBI's July 2026 framework, distributors who already hold valid NISM V-A and NISM Series XIII certificates are not required to take V-D to distribute SIFs. Check the latest NISM or AMFI clarification for your case.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Is there a free NISM 5D mock test?</h3></summary>
                                <p>Yes. We give a <a href="/demo/NISM-Series-V-D-Mutual-Fund---Specialized-Investment-Fund-Distributors-Certification-Examination/1273" data-track="free_demo">free demo test</a> so you can check our question quality before you pay. The full package gives 2,100+ questions with answers explained, 4 full-length 150-question tests, video lectures and short notes.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>What do I get in the Clear All Exams NISM V-D package?</h3></summary>
                                <p>You get 2,100+ practice questions with answers explained, 4 full-length 150-question mock tests that follow the official marks pattern, video lectures, short notes and an instant score report. Plans cost ₹1,399 for 15 days or ₹1,599 for 30 days. No hidden charges.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>How can I prepare for the NISM V-D exam in 15 days?</h3></summary>
                                <p>Days 1–6: learn the Mutual Fund module, which carries 68 marks. Days 7–11: learn Equity Derivatives and Interest Rate Derivatives and practise the calculations. Days 12–15: take full 150-question timed tests and revise weak chapters from the notes.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Can I use a calculator or Excel in the NISM V-D exam?</h3></summary>
                                <p>Test centre computers have Microsoft Excel or LibreOffice for calculations. Practise NAV, futures pricing, option value and bond duration sums in a spreadsheet before the exam.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>How long is the NISM V-D certificate valid and how do I renew it?</h3></summary>
                                <p>The certificate is valid for 3 years. To renew it, pass the NISM Series V-D exam again before your current certificate expires.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Can I take the mock tests on my mobile phone?</h3></summary>
                                <p>Yes. Tests, videos and notes work in any browser on mobile, tablet or computer. No app is needed.</p>
                            </details>
                            <details>
                                <summary><h3>Is Clear All Exams affiliated with NISM?</h3></summary>
                                <p>No. Clear All Exams is an independent preparation platform. We are not connected with NISM or SEBI. Only NISM handles exam registration and certificates.</p>
                            </details>
                        </div>
                    </section>

